<p>Seconding this, and adding that it should be listed in the containment procedures with the radio itself. You can also take out the &quot;never change it without permission&quot; part: Anything in the containment procedures is automatically something you never change without a <em>very</em> good reason. It makes sense to include a side note like that if it's something that could require occasional deviation and/or is really, really important not to deviate from<sup class="footnoteref"><a id="footnoteref-216597-1" href="javascript:;" class="footnoteref" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.utils.scrollToReference('footnote-216597-1')">1</a></sup>, but in this case it wouldn't be world-ending and there's no real reason for it to ever be changed.</p>
<p>There's still some rough edges here and there you can sand out as you get more feedback, but overall <em>much</em> improved from the previous posting. +1</p>
