				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/coocoocachoo" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(3011184); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=3011184&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1608608281" alt="CooCooCachoo" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=3011184)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/coocoocachoo" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(3011184); return false;" >CooCooCachoo</a></span> <span class="odate time_1490189685 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">22 Mar 2017 13:34</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-2773092">
									

<p>It's weird and strange - and that's a good thing. It caught my interest and made me read through and through. There's a few nitpicks I have with the clincal tone; such as making a reference to a species (domestic cat) but not giving us binomial nomenclature (<em>felis catus</em>). Otherwise, the containment and descriptions are enjoyable.</p>
<p>However, the interview&#8230; At the risk of giving conflicting advice I now think you've gone too far in the other direction. Now it seems the researcher is coddling the SCP, but that's my subjective opinion. Here's the line in particular I take issue with:</p>
<p>&quot;<strong>You don't have to escape. You're safe here in containment.</strong> We just want to understand you. If you cooperate, we can better understand each other. That's what you want, right? To understand humans?&quot;</p>
<p>My emphasis. I don't know it just&#8230;.it just doesn't strike me as something a Foundation Dr. would say to a non-humanoid SCP, especially one so recently contained. I think you can strike a middle ground in tone with that line (&quot;I'm sorry but we can't let that happen&quot; or &quot;You're not imprisoned, we're only trying to study you.&quot;) Remember, Foundation researchers and doctors have lied before/told half-truths to the SCP about the nature of their containment.</p>
<p>I have a few other nitpicks; having &quot;repeating the initial phrase&quot; in parenthesis is, to me, not needed. We can read, of course, that the SCP is doing precisely that. Also, as someone mentioned, if you want to give an interview transcript a feeling of time, in the (silence) portions, you should indicate a time. I.e: [SCP-XXXX is silent for 45 seconds].</p>
<p>All-in-all it held my interest and curiousity to the end. +1 from me. Nothing but nitpicks really stop me from enjoying the article, so well done.</p>

							</div>

								
